\par\par \uc2 Business/Financial Desk; SECTB\par \b \uc2 Yelp\uc2  Will Pay Workers' Travel for  \highlight22\uc2 Abortion \highlight\uc2  Access\b0\par\par\uc2 By Alisha Haridasani Gupta and Lauren Hirsch \par \uc2 736 \uc2 words\par \uc2 13 April 2022\par \uc2 The New York Times\par \uc2 NYTF\par \uc2 Late Edition - Final\par 4\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 Copyright 2022 The New York Times Company.  All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 The company has relatively few workers in Texas, which has the most restrictive \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  law.\par \par \uc2 Yelp\uc2  announced on Tuesday that it would cover expenses for its employees and their spouses who must travel out of state for \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  care, becoming the latest company to respond to a Texas law that bans the procedure after about six weeks of pregnancy.\par \par \uc2 The online search and review platform, which is based in San Francisco and has more than 4,000 workers, employs just over 200 in Texas, but the benefit extends to employees in other states who might be affected by ''current or future action that restricts access to covered \b \highlight22\uc2 reproductive health\b0 \highlight\uc2  care,'' a company representative said.\par \par \uc2 Last month, \uc2 Citigroup\uc2  became the first major bank to disclose that it will pay travel costs for employees affected by the law in Texas, where it has over 8,000 workers. Other companies that have announced policies aimed at mitigating the impact of the law include \uc2 Uber\uc2  and \uc2 Lyft\uc2 , which offered to pay legal fees for Texas drivers who could be sued for taking someone to an \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  clinic.\par \par \uc2 A Texas legislator warned \uc2 Citigroup\uc2  that he would introduce a bill to prevent the bank from underwriting municipal bonds in the state unless it rescinded its expense policy. While ''backlash gets a lot more attention,'' \uc2 Yelp\uc2  is not concerned about how its program, which starts next month, will be received, said Miriam Warren, the company's chief diversity officer. She and other executives have received many personal notes thanking \uc2 Yelp\uc2  for taking a stand on \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 , she said.\par \par \uc2 The move, made as companies vie for talent in a tight labor pool, will help \uc2 Yelp\uc2  maintain a more diverse and inclusive work force, Ms. Warren said. ''We want to be able to recruit and retain employees wherever they might be living,'' she said.\par \par \uc2 ''The ability to control your \b \highlight22\uc2 reproductive health\b0 \highlight\uc2 , and whether or when you want to extend your family, is absolutely fundamental to being able to be successful in the workplace,'' she added.\par \par \uc2 Questions about \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  access or vaccine mandates would have once been considered outside the realm of a corporate leader. But executives increasingly find they have to take a stand on such divisive issues because they are often of great importance to their workers and customers.\par \par \uc2 ''I think the question for these companies is really going to be: Where do you want to locate?'' said Caitlin Myers, an economist at \uc2 Middlebury College in Vermont\uc2  who has been tracking the economic effects of \b \highlight22\uc2 reproductive health\b0 \highlight\uc2  policies. ''Do you locate in a place where women have extraordinarily limited \b \highlight22\uc2 reproductive rights\b0 \highlight\uc2 ? Are you going to be able to recruit women to come there?''\par \par \uc2 Yelp\uc2 's travel benefit is part of its longer-term efforts on \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  access. In 2018, the company said it would do more to make sure \uc2 Yelp\uc2  users clearly understood the difference between \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  clinics and ''crisis pregnancy centers,'' which aim to steer people away from terminating a pregnancy.\par \par \uc2 ''Our User Operations team manually reviewed more than 2,000 businesses and clinics to ensure accurate categorization,'' \uc2 Yelp\uc2  said in a statement. Last year, when Texas passed its \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  law, the company also pledged to double-match employee donations to organizations that were fighting the legislation.\par \par \uc2 Under the new policy, \uc2 Yelp\uc2  employees will be able to submit receipts for travel expenses directly to their health insurance company, Ms. Warren said. ''So no one else at \uc2 Yelp\uc2  is ever going to know who is accessing this, or how or when, and it will be a reimbursement that comes through the insurance provider directly,'' she said.\par \par \uc2 The median income at \uc2 Yelp\uc2  was $92,000 in 2020, according to regulatory filings, and companies where employees earn higher wages are often the most vocally opposed to legal restrictions on \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 . Yet those restrictions disproportionately affect lower-income women who cannot afford the extra travel or the days off work to make the trip, Professor Myers said.\par \par \uc2 ''Affluent women and women with college educations aren't the ones who can't travel,'' she said. ''Those women will find a way to get to a place where it's still legal.''\par \par \uc2 Yelp said it would extend its new benefit to workers in any state ''that restricts access to covered \uc2  care.'' (PHOTOGRAPH BY JIM WILSON/THE NEW YORK TIMES) \par \par \uc2 Document NYTF000020220413ei4d0004x\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw284\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal4260\pichgoal600
