\par\par \uc2 National Desk; SECTA\par \b \uc2 Maryland Overrides Veto To Expand  \highlight22\uc2 Abortion \highlight\uc2  Access\b0\par\par\uc2 By Giulia Heyward \par \uc2 509 \uc2 words\par \uc2 11 April 2022\par \uc2 The New York Times\par \uc2 NYTF\par \uc2 Late Edition - Final\par 12\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 Copyright 2022 The New York Times Company.  All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 The new law allows trained medical professionals other than physicians to perform abortions and requires insurance providers to cover more costs.\par \par \uc2 Maryland is joining 14 other states in allowing trained medical professionals other than physicians to perform abortions. That change is part of a bill expanding \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights that was passed Saturday by state lawmakers, overriding the veto of Gov. \uc2 Larry Hogan\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Under the new law, which will take effect July 1, nurse practitioners, nurse midwives and trained physician assistants will be able to perform abortions. The law will also require most insurance providers in the state to cover the cost of an \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 , at no cost to the resident, and directs the state to invest $3.5 million a year into \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 -care training.\par \par \uc2 ''They stood up for health care, they stood up for access to \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  care -- which we believe is health care, and health care is a human right -- so they did what was right for the women in the state of Maryland,'' said Karen J. Nelson, the president and chief executive of Planned Parenthood of Maryland, referring to Maryland legislators.\par \par \uc2 Laura Bogley, the director of legislation for Maryland Right to Life, an anti-\b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  organization, said, ''This is an example of what happens when you have a partisan monopoly in a state legislature.'' She added, ''The monopoly breeds extremism.''\par \par \uc2 The new law in Maryland comes as many state legislators across the country are seeking to severely limit, or outright ban, access to \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 . State lawmakers enacted more \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  restrictions in 2021 than in any other year since the landmark 1973 Roe v. Wade decision, according to the \uc2 Guttmacher Institute\uc2 , an \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 -rights research organization. And research by the institute suggests that the country is poised to adopt more anti-\b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  restrictions this year. The Supreme Court is also expected to weaken, or even overturn, Roe by the summer.\par \par \uc2 When Mr. Hogan, a Republican, vetoed the bill on Friday, he wrote in an open letter to the speaker of Maryland's House of Delegates, Adrienne A. Jones, a Democrat, that allowing non-physicians to perform abortions would ''set back standards for women's health care and safety.''\par \par \uc2 But the House of Delegates overrode the veto by a vote of 90 to 46. The vote in the State Senate was 29 to 15.\par \par \uc2 Ms. Bogley said that she and others expect litigation challenging the constitutionality of the new law. ''That's not something the public supports nationally or in Maryland,'' she said.\par \par \uc2 Ms. Nelson maintained that the practice of allowing nonphysicians to perform abortions was normal in other states.\par \par \uc2 ''This is the standard of care in 14 other states,'' Ms. Nelson said. ''So Maryland, who typically is on the front end of \b \highlight22\uc2 reproductive health\b0 \highlight\uc2  care, actually had a little catching up to do here.''\par \par \uc2 Maryland House Speaker Adrienne Jones, a Democrat, received an open letter by the governor on Friday explaining his veto. (PHOTOGRAPH BY Brian Witte/Associated Press FOR THE NEW YORK TIMES) \par \par \uc2 Document NYTF000020220411ei4b0003u\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw284\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal4260\pichgoal600
