\par\par \uc2 Business/Financial Desk; SECTB\par \b \uc2 Finance; Texas Legislator Warns \uc2 Citigroup\uc2  Over  \highlight22\uc2 Abortion \highlight\b0\par\par\uc2 By Coral Murphy Marcos \par \uc2 309 \uc2 words\par \uc2 19 March 2022\par \uc2 The New York Times\par \uc2 NYTF\par \uc2 Late Edition - Final\par 2\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 Copyright 2022 The New York Times Company.  All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 A state representative threatened to introduce legislation that would bar local governments from doing business with companies that had such policies.\par \par \uc2 A Texas legislator warned \uc2 Citigroup\uc2  on Friday that he would introduce a bill to prevent the bank from underwriting municipal bonds in the state unless it rescinded its policy covering travel expenses for employees who go outside their state to seek an \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 State Representative \uc2 Briscoe Cain\uc2 , a Republican from the Houston area, wrote on \uc2 Facebook\uc2  and \uc2 Twitter\uc2  that the bill would bar local governments from doing business with any company ''that pays \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 -related expenses of its employees or that provides \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  coverage as an employee benefit.'' He said he had sent a cease-and-desist letter to \uc2 Citigroup\uc2 's chief executive, \uc2 Jane Fraser\uc2 , calling the policy a ''misuse of shareholder money.''\par \par \uc2 Citigroup\uc2  stated in a filing on Tuesday that it would provide travel benefits to employees seeking abortions outside their state, ''in response to changes in \b \highlight22\uc2 reproductive health\b0 \highlight\uc2  care laws in certain states.'' Last year, Texas enacted a law that bans \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  after about six weeks of pregnancy. The law took effect in September.\par \par \uc2 Citigroup\uc2  has 8,500 employees in Texas. Other companies, including \uc2 Salesforce\uc2  and Uber, have also announced policies in opposition to the \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  law.\par \par \uc2 Mr. Cain also vowed to propose legislation that, if passed, would authorize district attorneys from anywhere in the state to prosecute a company that violated the \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  law if the local district attorney did not take action.\par \par \uc2 Representatives of \uc2 Citigroup\uc2  could not be reached for comment Friday night.\par \par \uc2 State Representative Briscoe Cain said on Friday that he had sent a cease-and-desist letter to Citigroup's chief executive. (PHOTOGRAPH BY Jay Janner/Austin American-Statesman, via USA Today Network FOR THE NEW YORK TIMES) \par \par \uc2 Document NYTF000020220319ei3j0003d\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw284\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal4260\pichgoal600
